 "frozen": "2026-08-16 median of 9 runs at 63e878f, SAMPLES=1500. RE-FROZEN, not adjusted to pass \u2014 two independent reasons, both measured. (1) THE BASELINE DESCRIBED NO LIVING SOURCE: it was frozen 2026-07-28, five days BEFORE this repo's first commit (6a4b59c, 08-02). billboard-nameplate-storm had drifted ~1.66x on normalized p50, and the gated p95_norm channel sat ON the 1.5x threshold \u2014 A/A control at FIXED source was 1.37-1.69x, red 7 of 12 runs. Bisected to TWO deliberate steps, neither a defect to revert: 2497a13 (08-06, Step 9 perf lab) = 1.25x, paired ABBA 8/8, of which the Facet/react MicroProfiler span now wrapping every flush is 1.055x, paired 9/10; and d7d0e42 (08-14, core:settle) = 1.12x, paired ABBA 10/10, which bought the measure-publish cycle 2 flushes->1 and 4 solves->2. NONE of the 08-15 work (tint-fill tag rule, hit_lift, native_scroll_binding, ADR-0035 preferred transparency, easing curves, UI.Foreign, zstack arrange) moved this scene \u2014 08-14 21:01 through 08-16 is flat at 0.34-0.39 normalized p50, inside the control spread \u2014 and the tint-fill 'newly painted nodes' theory is refuted directly: the scene censuses 3 nodes (Screen + 2 Text, no Box, no tint) and one iteration is 50 flushes and 50 settle passes producing exactly 2 adapter writes. It is a per-flush-overhead microbenchmark, not a paint benchmark. (2) THE SAMPLE COUNT MOVED, 300 -> 1500, which shifts every p95: see the block comment on SAMPLES in tools/lune/bench.luau. That change took the worst gate-eligible A/A spread from 2.07x (textinput-typing-storm, ABOVE the 1.5x factor and therefore un-adjudicable) to 1.22x. Re-freeze with 9 runs and re-measure the A/A spread whenever WARMUP/SAMPLES/REGRESSION_FACTOR change. See docs/lessons/the-bench-heap-number-is-collector-phase.md",
